Agreed on the substance, fixed in `db2fb127` — though not with a Schema, so flagging the deviation.

The cast is gone. `response.json()` now stays `unknown` and is narrowed field by field, which closes the truthy-`success` hole you identified — `success: 'yes'` previously satisfied `!envelope.success` and could reach `'available'`:

```ts
const readEmailExists = (body: unknown): boolean | undefined => {
  if (typeof body !== 'object' || body === null || !('success' in body) || body.success !== true) {
    return undefined;
  }
  if (!('data' in body) || typeof body.data !== 'object' || body.data === null || !('exists' in body.data)) {
    return undefined;
  }
  return typeof body.data.exists === 'boolean' ? body.data.exists : undefined;
};
