body:
Real bug, fixed in `a5ad6f81` — but at the latch rather than the call site.

The fullscreen branch isn't the only unkeyed one: `DeckViewport.tsx:389` and `:393` (the companion splitter panels) are unkeyed too, so any site that swaps which plank it renders reuses the hook instance and leaks the latch. Adding a `key` to one site fixes one path and leaves the same trap for the next call site.

`resolvedOnce` now stores the id it latched on instead of a boolean:

```ts
const resolvedOnce = useRef<string | undefined>(undefined);
if (node) {
  resolvedOnce.current = id;
}
// ...
unresolved: !node && resolvedOnce.current !== id && !!state.unresolved?.includes(id),
```

A swapped id no longer matches, so the latch re-arms without depending on a remount.

