body:
Good catch, fixed in 847d5a5a. `reserved 2;` alone only protects the wire number — a later field could still take the name `echo_replicator` back and silently break JSON and text-format compatibility for anything that had serialized it. Both are reserved now, and the comment says why rather than just restating what the keyword does:

```proto
/// Field 2 held `echo_replicator`, the classical Automerge edge transport, removed once
/// Subduction became the only edge replicator. Both the number and the name are reserved so
/// neither can be reused: a new field reusing the name would break JSON/text compatibility.
reserved 2;
reserved "echo_replicator";
```

Split across two statements because protobuf does not allow numbers and names in the same `reserved`.

