body:
Not adding one — the plugin group already gets released by the ripple, and a second changeset would break two of this repo's rules.

I ran `changeset version` with only this PR's changeset present in `.changeset/` (everything else moved aside), on a clean tree, then reverted:

```
@dxos/app-framework          0.11.1 -> 0.12.0     group A, the declared minor
@dxos/react-ui-form          0.11.1 -> 0.12.0     group A, lockstep
@dxos/ui-types               0.11.1 -> 0.12.0     group A, lockstep
@dxos/storybook-addon-logger 0.11.1 -> 0.12.0     group A, lockstep
@dxos/plugin-game            0.11.1 -> 0.11.2     group B, dependent ripple
@dxos/plugin-settings        0.11.1 -> 0.11.2     group B, dependent ripple
@dxos/plugin-registry        0.11.1 -> 0.11.2     group B, dependent ripple
```

Every affected package publishes. Group B plugins depend on `@dxos/app-framework` via `workspace:*`, and with `updateInternalDependencies: "patch"` in `.changeset/config.json` they take a patch bump as dependents; being a `fixed` group, all 106 move in lockstep.

This is the documented design, not an accident — [`agents/instructions/changesets.md`](https://github.com/dxos/dxos/blob/main/agents/instructions/changesets.md) says "naming any one member bumps the whole group — never enumerate a group, and never name a downstream dependent (the ripple bumps dependents automatically; a Group A change also patch-bumps Group B)".

Adding a plugin changeset would also fail CI: `pnpm check-changesets` enforces one changeset per PR (`scripts/check-changesets.mjs`, the `count` rule).

