body:
Returning here skips the full-poll bookkeeping, so one namespace that keeps failing stops every other space from being polled.

While `hadPullFailure` holds, the chain below never runs: `#lastFullPoll` is not refreshed and `#resetSpacesToPoll()` is not called, so `#spacesToPoll` shrinks to the failing space and healthy spaces are polled again only through a `FeedAdvanced` hint, or never against a server that does not push hints. Before this change the failing space spun, but the full poll still fired on its interval.

Keeping the chain and swapping only the immediate re-poll for the back-off keeps both behaviours:

```ts
const scheduleNext = hadPullFailure ? () => this.#schedulePollRetry() : () => this.#pollTask.schedule();
if (!hadPullFailure) {
  this.#pullFailureBackoffMs = DEFAULT_FAILURE_BACKOFF_MS;
}
if (this.#lastFullPoll == null || Date.now() - this.#lastFullPoll > this.#currentPollingInterval) {
  this.#resetSpacesToPoll();
  scheduleNext();
} else if (this.#spacesToPoll.size > 0) {
  scheduleNext();
} else {
  // unchanged
