Done in `94b7dd87` — `DisplaceChannel`:

```ts
class DisplaceChannel {
  readonly #channel: BroadcastChannel;

  /**
   * Called when another worker posts `stop`. Assignable because what a stop means to this worker
   * changes as it starts up — before the storage lock is granted there is nothing to stand down from.
   */
  onStop: () => void = () => {};

  constructor(channelName: string) { … }
  postStop(): void { … }
  close(): void { … }
}
```

The action-name check against `DISPLACE_MESSAGE` now lives inside the class, so `run` reads as `channel.onStop = …` / `channel.postStop()` and never touches `postMessage` or `event.data`. The exported `displace()` helper goes through the same class rather than building its own `BroadcastChannel`, so the wire format has one definition.

Verified: `worker-framework:test-browser` 40/40, `worker-framework:test` 36/36, `tsc --noEmit` clean, lint clean.

