Done in afef619e. One thing worth flagging: two of the three names were already taken, so the migration renames an incumbent.

**`name` / `version`** replace `registryKey`, taken from the entity's own `meta.key` / `meta.version` rather than re-parsed out of the key the client composed — one source of truth, with the wire key as the fallback for an entity carrying no metadata of its own. The name is canonicalised to the `dxn:` form so a bare and a prefixed meta key land on the same row.

The payoff is in the lookups: an unversioned key is now an equality match, so the LIKE-prefix scan and its metacharacter escaping are gone entirely.

```diff
-              splitRegistryKey(key) === undefined
-                ? sql`(registryKey = ${key} OR registryKey LIKE ${escapeVersionPrefix(key)} ESCAPE '\\')`
-                : sql`registryKey = ${key}`
+              const { name, version } = splitRegistryKey(key);
+              return version === '' ? sql`name = ${name}` : sql`(name = ${name} AND version = ${version})`;
```

**`origin`**, not `source` — `objectMeta.source` is already the relation source EID from `0001_init`, read across QueryExecutor and the reverse-ref traversal, so renaming it would have reached well past this PR. `origin` holds `automerge` / `feed` / `registry`, typed as a `Schema.Literals` union so a SQL row needs no cast to narrow. Both space sources set it, so the column means what it says rather than only marking registry rows; every space-scoped scan now excludes on `origin != 'registry'` instead of `registryKey != ''`.

**The one rename:** `version` was taken by the monotonic counter the primary pass stamps on every write. That is renamed to `seq` — what it has always been — to free the name. SQLite rewrites dependent index definitions as part of `RENAME COLUMN`, so `idx_object_index_version` would have silently become an index on `seq`; it is dropped and recreated under the right name.

```sql
ALTER TABLE objectMeta RENAME COLUMN version TO seq;
DROP INDEX IF EXISTS idx_object_index_version;
CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_object_index_seq ON objectMeta(seq);
ALTER TABLE objectMeta ADD COLUMN name TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT '';
ALTER TABLE objectMeta ADD COLUMN version TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT '';
ALTER TABLE objectMeta ADD COLUMN origin TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'automerge';
ALTER TABLE objectMeta ADD COLUMN contentHash TEXT;
CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_object_index_origin ON objectMeta(origin);
CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_object_index_name_version ON objectMeta(name, version);
```

Still one migration — `0008` has never shipped, so there is nothing in the field to upgrade.

Local regression, all green (`pnpm format` and lint clean):

```
index-core:test         8 files,  65 passed
echo-host:test         26 files, 384 passed
echo-client:test       36 files, 588 passed
echo-client-e2e:test   20 files, 390 passed   (registry suite 25/25)
protocols:test          7 files,  33 passed
```

Say the word if you'd rather have the bare `source` and I'll do the `relationSource` rename too.

