Done in 53a15e4f — `RegistryEntry` is just the JSON now.

```ts
export const RegistryEntry = Schema.Struct({
  objectJson: Schema.String,
});
```

The host reads the entity's own `@meta` to file it. I checked what actually reaches the wire before relying on it, and a type carries its typename and version there too, so one rule covers every case:

```json
// a type entity
{ "id": "…", "@type": "dxn:org.dxos.type.schema:0.1.0",
  "@meta": { "keys": [], "key": "com.example.type.widget", "version": "0.1.0" } }
```

An entity with no `meta.key` is named after its EID. `registryEntryKey` and its `DXN`/`EID` imports are deleted, and with them the second source of truth for what an entity is called.

**One thing this shifted that was worth fixing properly.** Moving the key inside the JSON meant `submit` had to parse before it could look anything up — so every push re-parsed the whole registry, where before an unchanged entry was skipped on its digest. That is the common case for a snapshot protocol, and it cost enough to surface as a real failure: `echo-client`'s `strong-deps-stall` test went red under full-suite load (it passed 8/8 in isolation, and 588/588 on the branch without this change — so it was mine, not a flake).

Since the identity is a function of the content, the source now remembers which identity each digest a client sent resolved to, and an unchanged entry is recognised without being parsed again:

```ts
const known = filed.get(hash);
if (known !== undefined && this.#entries.get(known)?.contributions.get(clientId)?.hash === hash) {
  seen.add(known);
  refiled.set(hash, known);
  continue;
}
```

The map is replaced wholesale per submit rather than merged, so a digest a snapshot stopped carrying cannot resurrect the identity it used to name. `echo-client` is back to 588 passed.

The validation tests moved with the protocol — "an entry with an empty key" is no longer expressible, so that case is now "an entity carrying no key of its own cannot address the ordinary index", asserting it lands under `echo:///<id>` rather than under the empty name every ordinary row holds.

