body:
Agreed — it is, now. efc67f70 deletes `#execCompiled` and `#execInMemory` entirely; there is one `execQuery` and no branch on the mode:

```ts
if (!this.#planned) {
  this._plan = await this._runInRuntime(this.#planner.compilePlan(this._query));
  this.#planned = true;
}
const { workingSet, trace } = await this._execPlan(this._plan, []);
```

A `SqlStep` is reached through `_execStep` like every other step. `mode` is no longer state — it reports whether the plan the planner produced contains a `SqlStep`. The `#compilable` flag and the separate compiled-result cache are gone, so both paths share one change-detection and one `getResults()`.

